From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:25:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: keep the finished-job list's capacity on
 every pass

take_finished moved the engine's preallocated finished list out of the
engine with mem::take, and the job worker returned it only on a pass
that had signalled something. A pass that found nothing finished dropped
it, leaving a zero-capacity list, and the next finished job hit
push_within_capacity's expect: the p2 candidate panicked 19 s into boot
under ordinary desktop traffic (tmp/codex-hw/prep-p2-candidate-20261024).

Collect finished jobs in place with g16_finished::collect, into the
list the engine keeps. The worker takes the list only when it holds jobs
to signal, and always puts it back before relocking.

Make the bounds fail closed instead of panicking or failing the device:
if the finished list or the engine's job list is ever full, the jobs
that don't fit stay queued for a later pass, and a warning is printed
once.

Host tests: g16_finished (a 200,000-pass random model of the worker's
handoff never loses a job or capacity, a replay of the old handoff loses
the capacity and collect then defers instead of panicking, order and
partial collection), and source checks that the worker restores the list
and that take_finished, admit and run_job have no panics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
